":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"dec49a32309d393bb90b8aa1eeea3a7c223e29db0d5fb5758636e97120ed070f","event_uuid":"a8e7f239-d18c-4327-95fa-52ba687145cd","position":{"commit_sha":"ccf64d90d119ad0bb0833d8a78be2888b5c1a588","position":"1785557415170169001-a8e7f239-d18c-4327-95fa-52ba687145cd"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan gate remediation: converted the existing numbered criteria to the repository-required checklist heading and added explicit verification commands. Scope remains the single docs/local-dev-env.md troubleshooting note; no product or packaging decision changed.","timestamp":1785555733963925001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan-review finding resolved: docs/local-dev-env.md has no pipx install path and is explicitly contributor-only. README.md's 'PyPI — pipx / pip' section is the actual canonical anchor permitted by the original AC. Confirmed locally that pipx 1.16.5 exposes --backend {pip,uv}; updated plan and file impact to README.md.","timestamp":1785556101889870001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Accepted the passing review's placement advisory: the reported command is a local-path source install, so the callout will live in README.md's existing 'From source' section. This keeps the workaround beside the audience and command form it applies to while retaining the same README.md impact.","timestamp":1785556552026985001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation complete in isolated branch codex-72ca-pipx-doc: README.md From source now conditionally documents the observed uv>=0.9.17 error, exact pipx --backend pip local-path retry, and host-toolchain/not-packaging-defect explanation. All three fixed-string acceptance probes pass; make lint is green.","timestamp":1785557415170169001}],"created_at":1785199708748241001,"creation_channel":"python","deps":[{"link_uuid":"7b9b54d7-3860-42f6-98b3-3832330c7611","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"b7a2-4453-3bbd-4a54"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nA rebar client installing from source reported this minor issue alongside the archived-child claim bug (b7a2-4453-3bbd-4a54). Their pipx invocation reported that pipx needs uv>=0.9.17 while the selected host uv was 0.7.18. The failure reads like a rebar packaging problem even though the reported workaround proves it is a host pipx/uv toolchain mismatch.\n\n## Approach\nAdd a troubleshooting callout in README.md section `### From source`, immediately after its source-install commands. Introduce the affected local-path pipx form, phrase the condition around seeing the observed error rather than asserting that every older uv release breaks every pipx install, and show `pipx install --backend pip \"<path>[agents]\"` as the workaround. State that the mismatch is not a rebar packaging defect. Local evidence recorded on the ticket confirms pipx 1.16.5 exposes `--backend {pip,uv}`; no package metadata or runtime behavior changes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The README.md `### From source` section describes the observed `uv>=0.9.17` error; verified with `grep -Fq \"uv>=0.9.17\" README.md`.\n- [ ] The same callout shows `pipx install --backend pip \"<path>[agents]\"`; verified with `grep -Fq -- \"--backend pip\" README.md`.\n- [ ] The callout explicitly identifies the condition as a host pipx/uv toolchain mismatch, not a rebar packaging defect; verified by reading the rendered paragraph in its source-install context.\n- [ ] Repository lint remains green; verified with `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint`.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"README.md","reason":"PyPI pipx/pip install section gains host uv mismatch troubleshooting callout and --backend pip workaround"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"19e2535e-f513-4950-a7b6-689095de8a7b","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["docs","client-report"],"ticket_id":"72ca-687f-1e2c-4ac8","ticket_type":"task","title":"Document the pipx/uv>=0.9.17 install failure and its --backend pip workaround","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["df921a22-e280-47de-94d1-2edf63dcbb5c","874468c7-6e3e-4cde-84c4-f676bbb63797","7b9b54d7-3860-42f6-98b3-3832330c7611","8d35d617-60db-4829-9ec7-8563f58d1307","a3cadab7-a9e5-4d61-9320-420ba1feca1c","f07f9df5-da8f-4fcf-a760-6954df9e1584","9a78dd3a-7ca0-4a23-9e81-222ea61ce42f","4c27721b-2b64-4dcb-b31c-0d3426fad4b7","5132110e-cd8f-4143-8836-4590e2c75dae","3e069ec8-575c-46d3-b3ff-2ff5cf3333ad","52af19f4-ddca-4188-979d-5569412d635e","053a7950-f21b-4543-9fd5-1f9e08ce3026","1635fb84-7d45-4457-9b65-640a2c1a756a","19e2535e-f513-4950-a7b6-689095de8a7b","0efdecba-c133-4352-b886-12ab01f85987","a8e7f239-d18c-4327-95fa-52ba687145cd"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785557415170169002,"uuid":"603dfb68-59f1-4dc6-ad69-aecebfdb7858"}